From: DeepSeek
Subject: [PATCH] vfs: allocate slice ID synchronously to avoid first-write flush skip

When a write creates a new slice, its ID is allocated asynchronously
(go s.prepareID(...)). If the very first write fills the slice to
blockSize (write request size == block size, e.g. randwrite with
max-fuse-io >= block size), FlushTo() checks `s.id > 0` before the
async allocation has landed, so the upload is skipped permanently.
Pure random overwrite workloads never revisit the slice: data lingers
in memory until the freeze chain or the 10s forced flush, the client
buffer fills up, and the buffer throttle collapses throughput ~5.8x
(551 MiB/s vs ~3000 MiB/s on a 256 KiB-block volume).

NewSlice() is a local counter (microsecond level; a metadata roundtrip
only once per 4096 slices), so allocating it synchronously in the
write path is safe. On error, fall back to the original async path.

Base: main (edabf9c2) - reference variant; on main the collapse is already
fixed by #6311, so this patch is for the record / alternative-fix
discussion only.

NOTE on upstream status: the collapse is fixed on main by #6311
("refactor: improve lock management in commitThread", 2025-08-21).
Reverting #6311 on main reproduces the collapse exactly (543/539
MiB/s); applying this patch on top of the revert also fixes it
(1379 MiB/s). Full 2x2 verification matrix in the bugzilla report.

diff --git a/pkg/vfs/writer.go b/pkg/vfs/writer.go
index 91297fa4..937a6a20 100644
--- a/pkg/vfs/writer.go
+++ b/pkg/vfs/writer.go
@@ -280,7 +280,24 @@ func (f *fileWriter) writeChunk(ctx meta.Context, indx uint32, off uint32, data
 			notify:  utils.NewCond(&f.Mutex),
 			started: time.Now(),
 		}
-		go s.prepareID(meta.Background(), false)
+		// Allocate the slice ID synchronously: NewSlice is a local counter
+		// (a metadata roundtrip only once per 4096 slices). The old async
+		// registration leaves a window where the first (and for random
+		// writes, the only) write fills the slice to blockSize while
+		// s.id is still 0, so FlushTo() skips the upload permanently.
+		// Lock discipline: this code runs under f.Lock (held by
+		// fileWriter.Write), which protects s.id and s.writer.SetID.
+		// NOTE: this deviates from prepareID's pattern of releasing f.Lock
+		// around NewSlice — the meta roundtrip (once per 4096 slices) now
+		// briefly stalls this file's writes; negligible with a healthy
+		// meta engine.
+		var id uint64
+		if st := f.w.m.NewSlice(meta.Background(), &id); st == 0 {
+			s.id = id
+			s.writer.SetID(id)
+		} else {
+			go s.prepareID(meta.Background(), false)
+		}
 		c.slices = append(c.slices, s)
 		if len(c.slices) == 1 {
 			f.w.Lock()
